# Object.keys of an object with a layout looks the list of names up in a table of the run time, under the sum of the two words that say which fields the object has and in which order.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="names" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[point]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[shape]] = Load(b@[[point]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[order]] = Load(b@[[point]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:OrderWords)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[shape]], b@[[order]])
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = BitAnd(b@[[sum]], $1023(b@{{*}}))
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[sameShape]] = Equal(b@[[shape]], b@{{*}})
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[sameShape]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[sameOrder]] = Equal(b@[[order]], b@{{*}})
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[sameOrder]], Terminal)
# A hit makes the array in place: the cell is allocated and gets its header and the shared storage that holds the names. No name is copied.
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[array]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:SomeRegister, runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = SomeEarlyRegister, numGPScratchRegisters = 1, Terminal|Writes:{collectorState, AllocatorState}|Reads:{collectorState, AllocatorState})
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: #{{*}}, Rare:#
# CHECK: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[array]], ControlDependent|Writes:JSCell_header)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@{{*}}, b@[[array]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Writes:JSObject_butterfly)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# One call into the run time serves every miss. Object.keys cannot be replaced: nothing makes its function object or tests which function the member holds.
# CALLS-LABEL: name="names" role=Source
# CALLS-NOT: :CallBuiltin
# CALLS-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-NOT: ExitsSideways
# CALLS-LABEL: end of function
# The counts hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: instructions: 33, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 4
# ARM64: instructions: 33, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 6
